Algorithm 
Airport Facilities Using Prim’s Algorithm
Start.
Create a weighted graph in which vertices represent airport facilities and edges represent possible ground connections.
Input the number of vertices and the weights of the edges.
Initialize all vertices as unvisited and select a starting vertex.
Find the minimum-weight edge connecting a visited vertex to an unvisited vertex.
Select that edge and mark the new vertex as visited.
Repeat Steps 5 and 6 until all vertices are visited or no connecting edge is available.
Display all selected edges and their weights.
Calculate and display the total cost of the selected connections.
Stop.
